# Pin the on-disk line endings of the few files that are intentionally
# CRLF (edited/run on the Windows production host — see CLAUDE.md's
# "Windows-isms are intentional" note). `-text` disables any newline
# normalization for these paths (no autocrlf mangling on checkout/checkin,
# no accidental LF flip from a tool that opens them in text mode), without
# renormalizing what's already committed. Every other tracked file in this
# repo is currently LF and is left alone.
distill.py -text
looker.py -text
